recorded 2026-11-12 9.0.10 neutralized
The T049 recording of StartCLI "trace --download" with the 9.0 client on a non-production 9.0.10 server without a cluster: exit 0, 8 stdout lines without an n-OK prefix, one JVM line on stderr. Mirrors the recording: the exit code, the order and wording of the stdout lines (JAVA_HOME notice, the SECURITY WARNING three times, the REST client's log4j "ERROR ... DnsServerAddressStreamProviders ..." netty notice for macOS, the "Password: " prompt, the "Trace data (<n> MB) stored to: <path>" line with <n> in MiB with three decimals, an empty last line) and the single "Picked up JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS" stderr line. Invented (research D-21): the time in the log4j line, the download path, the trust-store path, and the whole ok.log, which is the fictitious 8.1-shaped log of the reconstructed case (acme classes, node1, *.example.test, fictitious secrets in one Authorization header and one <password> element) instead of the recorded 27,336-byte warn-level trace log; <n> = 0.004 matches its size (4,224 bytes).
The recorded 9.0 entry lines have the 8.1 layout (<LEVEL> dd.MM.yy HH:mm:ss,SSS [<thread>] ...); at the recorded level warn most lines were tab-indented stack-trace lines, which the fictitious ok.log does not imitate.
